---
description: Rules for the Expo app
globs: apps/mobile/src/**/*.ts,apps/mobile/src/**/*.tsx,apps/mobile/app.json,apps/mobile/babel.config.js,packages/ui/src/**/*.tsx
alwaysApply: false
---

**React Compiler is ON.** Never write `useMemo`, `useCallback` or `memo` — manual memoisation is a bug
here, not an optimisation.

**Animation:** `react-native-reanimated` only. Never import `Animated` or `Easing` from `react-native`.
On Reanimated 4 use `sharedValue.get()` / `sharedValue.set(…)`, not `.value`.

**Styling:** every colour, size, radius, spacing and type role comes from the generated tokens (`tokens` and
`rn()` from `@bbc/ui`, made from `DESIGN.md` by `bun run tokens`). `src/constants/club.ts` (the `Club` object)
holds the entry's own colours, spacing and radii, written by hand so a token change does not reach them
(ADR-IMPL-047) — the entry's type roles and `ClubButton` still read the tokens. The entry screens read it; outside
them only the root's dark chrome and the phone column's width (`Club.layout.phoneMaxWidth`). No inline hex, no
`rgba(...)`, no magic numbers. If a token is missing, say so — do not invent one. Where `DESIGN.md` and Figma
disagree, Figma wins (ADR-IMPL-046); report the conflict.

**Typography roles** (do not swap them): `display`/`headline`/`title` are Fraunces (serif); body text is
Geist; flight facts and field labels are Geist Mono, uppercase for labels.

**Status bar:** the root shows light glyphs (the entry, Welcome). A screen on the porcelain page, a photograph
or the night mounts `<ScreenStatusBar on="light" | "dark" />` (`src/components/screen-status-bar.tsx`) for the
surface under the bar.

**Android Back:** a `ModalSheet` closes itself on Back. A screen with states of its own (typing, an expanded
sheet, a second step) handles `BackHandler` as its Cancel or Done does.

**Every interactive element needs `testID="screen.element"`** (`signIn.submit`, `verify.code`,
`setPassword.continue`). Maestro flows depend on these names.

**Accessibility:** `accessibilityRole` and `accessibilityLabel` on everything tappable; tap targets ≥ 44 pt
(use `hitSlop` on text links).

**Navigation:** Expo Router. Route params carry `email` and `purpose` only — never `otp`, `code`, `token`
or `password` (Expo Router serialises params into the URL on web and into persisted state everywhere).
A one-time code lives in component state or in `src/features/auth/otp-holder.ts`, which is cleared when the
auth stack unmounts.

**Forbidden imports:** `@bbc/db`, `@bbc/platform`, `@bbc/api`, anything under `isolated/` or
`packages/modules/`; `@react-native-async-storage/async-storage` (use MMKV for cache, `expo-secure-store`
for secrets); `react-native-fast-image` (use `expo-image`).

**Never run the app yourself** (`expo start`, `expo run:ios`, simulators). Produce the code and give the
commands for the human to run.
